From e5b0bb59710d0a92951a84b7e521f480ed9d0d68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steelhead99x <steelhead99x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:18:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(bench): leave aws-lc-rs rows out on Xtensa and bare
 metal

aws-lc names no Xtensa CPU in include/openssl/target.h, so aws-lc-sys
fails with "Unknown target CPU" for xtensa-esp32s3-espidf, and it needs an
operating system, so it does not build for thumbv7em-none-eabihf either.
Gate each aws-lc-rs row on not(any(target_arch = "xtensa",
target_os = "none")), as graviola's rows are gated on the architectures it
supports, and pass helpers `()` for its algorithm there through an `aws!`
macro, so every other row builds unchanged.

Co-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
